From 8050e1ff200613676f4ac39de755b6081ba5fd5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:31:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/47] NMXVGAFB: virtio-gpu blob scan-out (virtio-vga
 blob=true), VGA BAR as the fallback

A small virtio 1.x transport (modern PCI capabilities, one polled control queue) for QEMU's virtio-vga.
With blob resources offered, the scan-out moves from the VGA BAR into a contiguous guest-RAM buffer
shown on scanout 0 as a guest blob, which QEMU hands to its GL display as a dmabuf; the VBL timer
flushes it. Without blob support (or on any failure) the device is reset and the VGA BAR stays the
scan-out, as before; -nmxvgafbnovirtio skips it. Tested: the fallback on a device without blob
(host scanout reported 2880x1710, desktop composited on the VF as before).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DP5dwQG4pUvK6V9ftNsQRB
